Register the playerbot "say" strategy so combat chatter can fire at all.

Touches: modules/mod-playerbots/src/Ai/Base/StrategyContext.h,
         modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/Factory/AiFactory.cpp
         (AiFactory::AddDefaultCombatStrategies)

Why: SayStrategy (say::taunt, say::aoe, say::low health, say::low mana,
say::critical health) and SayAction have existed in the module since the
start, but StrategyContext never had a "say" creator and AiFactory never
added the strategy to any engine, so none of its triggers ever ran and
no bot ever said a taunt. Bug report #176 ("generate or add a bunch of
funny things for playerbots to say -- don't be afraid to use language
like 'glass that cunt!'") is half a content job (new SQL lines) and half
this wiring job; without this patch the new taunt pool is as silent as
the old one. SayAction self-throttles (one line per ~30s, and after
anyone in the group speaks, every member's clock is pushed ~20s per
member index), and per-line chance weights live in
ai_playerbot_texts_chance (aoe lowered 75 -> 40, low health 100 -> 60,
low mana 100 -> 50, taunt kept at 30) so the lines stay occasional.

--- a/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Ai/Base/StrategyContext.h
+++ b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Ai/Base/StrategyContext.h
@@ includes
 #include "RunawayStrategy.h"
+#include "SayStrategy.h"
 #include "StayStrategy.h"
@@ StrategyContext::StrategyContext()
         creators["chat"] = &StrategyContext::chat;
+        creators["say"] = &StrategyContext::say;
         creators["default"] = &StrategyContext::world_packet;
@@ StrategyContext private factories
     static Strategy* chat(PlayerbotAI* botAI) { return new ChatCommandHandlerStrategy(botAI); }
+    static Strategy* say(PlayerbotAI* botAI) { return new SayStrategy(botAI); }

--- a/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/Factory/AiFactory.cpp
+++ b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/Factory/AiFactory.cpp
@@ AiFactory::AddDefaultCombatStrategies
     if (sPlayerbotAIConfig.autoAvoidAoe && facade->HasRealPlayerMaster())
         engine->addStrategy("avoid aoe", false);

     engine->addStrategy("formation", false);
+
+    // Report #176: combat chatter. The "say" strategy (taunt / aoe / low
+    // health / low mana one-liners from ai_playerbot_texts) existed in the
+    // module but was never registered in StrategyContext, so none of its
+    // triggers ever ran and every bot stayed silent in combat. SayAction
+    // self-throttles (one line per ~30s, and after anyone in the group
+    // speaks, everyone else's clock is pushed ~20s per member), and the
+    // per-line chance weights live in ai_playerbot_texts_chance.
+    engine->addStrategy("say", false);

     switch (player->getClass())
